{"id":"4f4cf861-948c-4510-9422-fb04c067a3e6","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"736e045b843e4511","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/theme-follow.ts","baseline":{"blob":"e425ec41c1b7baab22c96d4ad9419d7db8171178","start":522,"end":880},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","showVsCodeTheme","(","hub",":","Hub",")",":","(","(",")","=>","void",")","|","undefined","{","const","workbench","=","document",".","querySelector","<","HTMLElement",">","(","\"",".monaco-workbench","\"",")",";","if","(","workbench","===","null",")","{","return","undefined",";","}","followVsCodeTheme","(","workbench",")",";","const","publish","=","(",")",":","void","=>","{","hub",".","publish","(","\"","theme.colors","\"",",","readVsCodeColors","(","workbench",")",")",";","}",";","publish","(",")",";","return","publish",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"b720c8ff78bbd012","after":"f7713d84f3784995"}},"payload":{"text":"Web Awesome in the workbench's document, on the active VS Code theme, and its colours told to the shell; returns\nwhat tells them again (on each theme change: followSystemTheme). Nothing before the workbench is there.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:53:03.827Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:53:03.827Z"}
{"id":"d1d85b99-0a52-4c23-a873-876e935eeb7f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e05bb2f3a05c870f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/theme-follow.ts","baseline":{"blob":"d4f43254a52f093c00fdb0ca4859975af93f2f30","start":1958,"end":1999},"shape":{"type":"MemberExpression","atoms":["vscode",".","window",".","onDidChangeActiveColorTheme"]},"context":{"before":"58d64226965340a8","after":"0e4caa586b292a1b"}},"payload":{"text":"(VS Code has swapped its theme's style when it says so; a frame later, its colours read as the new theme's)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:57.688Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:57.688Z"}
{"id":"e6d51318-0d2b-46c1-80a0-57f5f72fcf32","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"f7713d84f3784995","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/theme-follow.ts","baseline":{"blob":"657f28268175c3510fc4b7ee123c83c08e7c56bc","start":1110,"end":1777},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","followSystemTheme","(","vscode",":","typeof","vscodeApi",",","hub",":","Hub",",","publishColors",":","(",")","=>","void",")",":","void","{","const","apply","=","(","dark",":","boolean",")",":","void","=>","{","void","vscode",".","workspace",".","getConfiguration","(",")",".","update","(","\"","workbench.colorTheme","\"",",","dark","?","\"","Default Dark+","\"",":","\"","Default Light+","\"",",","vscode",".","ConfigurationTarget",".","Global",")",";","}",";","const","system","=","window",".","matchMedia","(","\"","(prefers-color-scheme: dark)","\"",")",";","vscode",".","window",".","onDidChangeActiveColorTheme","(","(",")","=>","{","requestAnimationFrame","(","publishColors",")",";","}",")",";","hub",".","subscribe","(","\"","theme.colorScheme","\"",",","(","data",")","=>","{","apply","(","(","data","as","{","\"","dark","\"","?",":","boolean","}","|","null",")","?.","dark","??","system",".","matches",")",";","}",")",";","system",".","addEventListener","(","\"","change","\"",",","(",")","=>","{","apply","(","system",".","matches",")",";","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"736e045b843e4511"}},"payload":{"text":"The colour theme follows the system: `window.autoDetectColorScheme` isn't wired to `prefers-color-scheme` in this\nmonaco-vscode-api build, so `workbench.colorTheme` is set here. The shell is the source of truth (it reliably gets\nprefers-color-scheme changes; an iframe may not), so what it publishes on `theme.colorScheme` is applied; this frame's\nown matchMedia is a fallback. Each theme change tells the shell VS Code's colours again (`publishColors`).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:53:02.646Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:53:02.646Z"}
{"id":"fdb7a40c-429e-4a6c-8b0f-7766471fba52","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/theme-follow.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9b45a8359f8a9bd1bbf1b1f15c0bca8a67437ced","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"e46e22f049b9d08c"}},"payload":{"text":"The editor's theme follows the system's, as the shell's does: Web Awesome in the workbench's document on the active\nVS Code theme (theme/vscode), VS Code's colours told to the shell so it draws in them (theme/vscode-colors), and the\ncolour theme switched to light or dark as the system's preference changes.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:53:10.909Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:53:10.909Z"}
